## CONTEXT BAND AND HANDOVER
At about 70% context start no new step. At about 75%, stop at a safe boundary: files whole, scratch copies discarded, every process you started stopped by pid, your containers, networks and volumes removed, the lock released. Then write `/Volumes/Datasec_DEV/!CODING/Datasec/Datasec Security Composer/1_Project_Definition/Briefs/2026-11-12_B1534_HANDOVER.md` (done / in hand / next / processes left / decisions a successor keeps: base sha, branch head if pushed, the base red set, the blobs, the Q-answers as stamped), last line `HANDOVER B1534: next step <n> | done steps <list>`, and end STATUS with the same line.

## HARD STOP (slot)
At the HARD STOP clock: start nothing new. Push nothing unproven. The push happens only after Steps 4, 5 and 7(a)-(g) are all green; otherwise end `STOPPED: <reason>` (or the HANDOVER) and push nothing.

## STANDING LINES
- **PRIOR-WORK CHECK** (Step 1; a READY without a PRIOR WORK section is returned). No message to any human. No comment, edit, close or review on any PR. **Jira: 0 reads, 0 writes by the seat.** Never delete (`rm`, `branch -d`, `--prune`, `gc`, `reset`, `clean`, `stash`, `checkout -- <file>`, `sed -i`); MOVE to `.tools/b1534/quarantine/`. Not run = NOT RUN. Source beats this kit. Never open `.local/`, `Source_Documents/**` or another seat's `.tools/*` (read-only copies of B1504 harness files from the committed evidence folder only).
- **Never hand-edit the lockfile.** A lock that is not what npm wrote in the pinned container is a finding, not something to fix by editing. A blob or entry that is not in the predicted set is a finding with both blobs printed, not something to adjust.
- **Closed lists** (the allowed paths, the changed lockfile entries, the commands): each is stated by its PROPERTY first and then "at least these"; any other shape: prove it meets the property or STOP.
- **Red/green is not applicable to a dependency bump** (no behaviour is added, no test is written); the proof is the Step 5 comparison (names lost 0), the builds, the install proof of Step 4 and the named alert set of Step 3c. Say that once in STATUS. `always-verify-and-check` and `no-skip-on-failure`: a red you cannot explain is a STOP; never skip a failing step.
- Shell: no `cd`; absolute single-quoted paths; `git -C ... --no-optional-locks` for reads; `/usr/bin/grep -i` with a positive control per count; python `-I -B`. Every count, `file:line` and clock in STATUS is printed by a program (`grep -n`, `awk NR`, `date`).
- **Git identity is never overridden.** The repo's own configured identity only, as the IDENTITY slot sets it in your clone; never `git -c user.name/user.email`, never `GIT_AUTHOR_*` / `GIT_COMMITTER_*`; your READY section prints `git log --format='%h %ae | %ce'` for the new commit, each email equal to the configured email.
- **Commit rules:** no ticket key, brief number, card id or person's name in any message or tracked line; exactly ONE trailer, the attribution line your own session reminder gives. No `.env`, no secret. ONE plain push of ONE ref.

